WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.760
For years, Marvel fans assumed Natalie Portman
was finished playing Jane Foster in the Marvel

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.050
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.200
That all changed at San Diego Comic-Con 2019,
when it was announced that she'd return to

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.230
wield Mjolnir as the Mighty Thor in 2021's
Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.230
But what brought her back to the MCU?

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.041
Natalie Portman was widely reported to be
unhappy with Marvel while filming Thor: The

00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:22.041
Dark World.

00:00:22.041 --> 00:00:26.090
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Portman
had championed director Patty Jenkins to helm

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.650
the movie and was shocked when Jenkins was
fired from the project.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.820
Portman wanted Jenkins to be the first female
director in the MCU and was blindsided by

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.910
Jenkins' termination, as she was allegedly
not told ahead of time and only learned of

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.180
it through news reports.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.690
Unable to leave the project due to contractual
obligations, Portman stuck it out and completed

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.600
The Dark World, but behind the scenes, she
may not have been shy about her feelings regarding

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.600
the whole ordeal.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.890
Still, in public, she never badmouthed Marvel.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:54.170
When asked about her relationship with the
company in interviews, she was always expertly

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.280
vague with her answers.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.920
Taika Waititi's Thor: Ragnarok is wildly different
from the first two Thor movies, which can't

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.470
help but seem stuffy and downright dour compared
to the visually splendid comedy feast Waititi

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.470
gave us.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.580
Let's face it, Thor can sometimes be a bit
boring.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.360
Sure, he's the God of Thunder, but he's also
been a kind of stick in the mud.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.330
Waititi, along with screenwriters Eric Pearson,
Craig Kyle, and Christopher L. Yost, managed

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:21.280
to keep the sweet innocence of Thor's character
but made him much more fun-loving and way

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.600
less stiff.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.600
"Baby!"

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.600
"Moron!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.910
You big child!"

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.240
"Thor go!"

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.220
"I am going!"

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.450
Thor comes into his own in Ragnarok, played
perfectly by Hemsworth, whose comedic chops

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.540
are on full display.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.310
Natalie Portman wasn't going to come back
to the Marvel fold for just anyone.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.110
Waititi's idea for a female Thor had to be
very attractive for Portman, and she must

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:45.909
trust Waititi's vision to want to sign back
up with the company she said she was "done"

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:47.310
with just a few years ago.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.860
"For the first time: Female Thor.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.720
Please, welcome to the stage, Natalie Portman!"

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.700
According to studio chief Kevin Feige, the
director won his new star over very quickly.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.700
He told CNN:

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.280
"We'd been in touch with Natalie.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.320
She's part of the MCU family and we put she
and Taika together.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.340
It took one meeting and she agreed to do it."

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.820
If only all creative decisions were so simple.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.200
Jane Foster is a world-renowned astrophysicist,
but she's often come off as a damsel in distress

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.730
in the MCU, so it's not a surprise Natalie
Portman spent years publicly ambivalent about

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:21.930
returning to the character.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.900
That, combined with the fallout from Marvel
firing Patty Jenkins, was more than enough

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:26.900
to keep her away.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.470
But being offered the chance to play Jane
Foster as the Mighty Thor provides Portman

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:33.120
with so much more than just being regarded
as Thor's ex-girlfriend.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.310
She gets to portray another female superhero
in the MCU.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:40.629
She won't be seen as merely a love interest
for Thor Odinson; she will be his equal.

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:44.510
Portman has used her previous appearances
as Dr. Jane Foster to inspire young women

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.569
around the world to get involved in the sciences,
so the thought of bringing Dr. Foster back

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:50.470
and being Thor must have been very appealing.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.150
Natalie Portman's Jane Foster has long been
one of the most powerful intellects in the

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:59.250
MCU, but it'd be tough to play a character
dubbed the Mighty Thor without adding some

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:03.290
brawn to that brainpower - and Portman is
already planning to buff up for her role in

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.290
Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.819
Shortly after Marvel's surprise Comic-Con
announcement, she took to social media to

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:11.780
express her enthusiasm for the project, posting
an Instagram update in which she pronounced

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.670
herself "thrilled" to share the news - and
promised to hit the gym for all that hammer-wielding

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.670
action.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.540
She quipped: "Remember this as the 'before'
picture for when I get jacked."

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.190
Will Portman be taking workout tips from Chris
Hemsworth?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:26.470
Only time will tell, but in the comics, Jane
Foster spent her time as the Mighty Thor wiping

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.220
the floor with a laundry list of powerful
adversaries that included such heavyweights

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:34.890
as Mangog, Malekith, the Phoenix Force, and
even Odin himself - it'll take one heck of

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:39.200
a gym regimen to prepare her for whatever
she's due to face in Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.769
Tom Petty warned us that the waiting is the
hardest part.

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:45.400
Thor: Love and Thunder hasn't even started
shooting yet.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.730
According to Movieweb, the film, which is
slated for release in November 2021, won't

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:54.000
begin production until the completion of Marvel's
Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.010
in 2020.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.670
This means we've got a very long wait ahead
of us before we get to see Natalie Portman

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.190
and the rest of the cast in the fourth Thor
movie.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.239
Marvel is very good at keeping secrets, so
don't expect to hear much from the set even

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:07.060
after it does finally start filming.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.010
But don't feel too bad, Marvel fans - the
studio will serve up a few movies to keep

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:15.890
us entertained until Thor: Love and Thunder
comes out, including Black Widow, The Eternals,

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.780
the aforementioned Shang-Chi and the Legend
of the Ten Rings, and Doctor Strange and the

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.310
Multiverse of Madness.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:25.430
Marvel also has plenty of upcoming television
shows slated to air on the Disney+ streaming

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.740
channel, including Loki starring Tom Hiddleston.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.100
Let the countdown to November 2021 begin!

